> Okay, I've now tested stock 2.6.7 without debian patches and the
> situation is the same: the sym53c8xx_2 driver doesn't work but fails on
> boot with messages about timeouts and resets.
>
> Has anyone had better experience with 2.6.x kernels on AS200?

I had this problem on a LX164 machine.  The problem seemed to be a 
missing CONFIG_ define which used to be in old versions of the kernel, 
but has disappeared in recent versions.  Unfortunately, quite a lot of 
the alpha code still expects it.

If I remember correctly, it was CONFIG_ALPHA_SRM.

My .config is attached, in case it helps.  This is from the 2.6.6 
kernel that I'm running on this machine.  You will need to change it, I 
suppose, as far as the actual machine type is concerned.

